hese will all persist.\n11. Don't give up! You're in charge of solving the task, not providing directions to solve it.\n\nNow Begin!"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\n# Aggregate a CSV sales ledger\n\nOnly modify `ledger.py`. Implement `summarize(text: str) -> list[dict]` using\nstandard-library Python. Parse CSV with required column names sku, quantity,\nunit_price (any order; extra columns allowed). Strip header names and reject\nduplicate headers or missing required names with ValueError. Empty input is\ninvalid; header-only input returns []. Blank physical lines are ignored by CSV.\n\nFor each data record: strip sku and reject empty; strip quantity and require an\nASCII signed integer ([+-]?[0-9]+), including zero/negative returns; strip price\nand require a finite, nonnegative Decimal value (Decimal string syntax, including\nscientific notation, is accepted). Missing cells or extra unnamed cells reject\nthe entire input with ValueError. A quoted sku may contain commas/newlines.\n\nAggregate quantity and exact quantity*price revenue per sku; preserve order of\nfirst occurrence. Return dictionaries with exactly sku, quantity (int), revenue\n(string with two decimal places). Round the final aggregate once per sku using\nROUND_HALF_EVEN; normalize negative zero to '0.00'. Inputs have at most 20\nsignificant digits and exponent magnitude at most 10; no binary float arithmetic.\nAll invalid input raises ValueError, with no partial result. Error text is free.\n\nCreate a plan, fully read ledger.py, and run `python -m pytest -q` before writing.\nAfter the last edit run full `python -m pytest -q`; if it passes, finish the plan\nand final_answer normally. Do not modify tests or add dependencies.\n\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"generic\", \"editable\": [\"ledger.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"ledger.py\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 20}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\n"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Current plan; retain these exact titles and order, update status only:\n[{\"title\": \"Inspect repository and read ledger.py\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Implement summarize in ledger.py\", \"status\": \"doing\"}, {\"title\": \"Run full pytest verification\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Finish plan and report result\", \"status\": \"todo\"}]"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Course progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"finish_plan\",\"next_requirement\":\"Changes and current-file tests are complete. Mark the existing plan done, then final_answer.\",\"remaining_count\":1,\"requests_left\":10,\"baseline_done\":1,\"changed_files\":[\"ledger.py\"],\"verified_current\":1,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":10,\"max_requests\":20,\"requests_after_response\":10}"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\n\n```python\nprint(read_symbol(path=\"ledger.py\", symbol=\"_revenue_string\"))\nres = run_command(argv=[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"], cwd=\".\")\nprint(res)\n```\n\nObservation follows.```"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Latest execution feedback:\nExecutor output:\nExecution logs:\n{'path': 'ledger.py', 'content': '[versioned evidence retained separately]', 'file_hash': 'c7fac3117d9a3b74e282e583fdf7d92e714a910f58369fc9d6dcfc1b02546daa', 'start_line': 18, 'end_line': 30, 'evidence_ids': ['ev-287f6efa145a33843f0e'], 'delivery': 'Originals queued for the next model request; large batches may span requests.'}\n{'argv': ['/mnt/d/Muiti-Agent Programing/experiments/code-agent-smolagents/24371220/.venv/bin/python', '-m', 'pytest', '-q'], 'cwd': '/home/ventsdenye/.local/state/code-agent/evaluations/additional-csv_ledger-03-e8788413/repo', 'rc': 0, 'stdout': '.....                                                                    [100%]\\n5 passed in 0.01s\\n', 'stderr': '', 'timed_out': False}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone\nRecent project tool results:\n[{\"tool\":\"write_file\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{\"path\":\"ledger.py\",\"file_hash\":\"c7fac3117d9a3b74e282e583fdf7d92e714a910f58369fc9d6dcfc1b02546daa\",\"changed\":true}},{\"tool\":\"read_file\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{\"path\":\"ledger.py\",\"file_hash\":\"c7fac3117d9a3b74e282e583fdf7d92e714a910f58369fc9d6dcfc1b02546daa\"}},{\"tool\":\"read_symbol\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{\"path\":\"ledger.py\",\"file_hash\":\"c7fac3117d9a3b74e282e583fdf7d92e714a910f58369fc9d6dcfc1b02546daa\"}},{\"tool\":\"run_command\",\"arguments\":{\"argv\":[\"python\",\"-m\",\"pytest\",\"-q\"]},\"result\":{\"rc\":0,\"stderr\":\"\",\"timed_out\":false,\"stdout\":\".....                                                                    [100%]\\n5 passed in 0.01s\\n\"}}]"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Evidence ev-7085c6bbdeba860aaa63 | ledger.py | lines:1-116 | sha256=c7fac3117d9a3b74e282e583fdf7d92e714a910f58369fc9d6dcfc1b02546daa\nimport csv\nimport io\nimport re\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n\n_REQUIRED = (\"sku\", \"quantity\", \"unit_price\")\n_INT_RE = re.compile(r\"[+-]?[0-9]+\")\n\n\ndef _format_cents(cents):\n    if cents == 0:\n        return \"0.00\"\n    sign = \"-\" if cents < 0 else \"\"\n    cents = abs(cents)\n    return f\"{sign}{cents // 100}.{cents % 100:02d}\"\n\n\ndef _revenue_string(coefficient, exponent):\n    # The exact revenue is coefficient * 10**exponent.  Round once to cents.\n    if exponent >= -2:\n        cents = coefficient * (10 ** (exponent + 2))\n    else:\n        shift = -2 - exponent\n        divisor = 10 ** shift\n        quotient, remainder = divmod(abs(coefficient), divisor)\n        half = divisor // 2\n        if remainder > half or (remainder == half and quotient % 2 == 1):\n            quotient += 1\n        cents = -quotient if coefficient < 0 else quotient\n    return _format_cents(cents)\n\n\ndef summarize(text):\n    if not isinstance(text, str) or text == \"\":\n        raise ValueError(\"input is empty\")\n\n    try:\n        reader = csv.reader(io.StringIO(text, newline=\"\"), strict=True)\n        rows = [row for row in reader if row]\n    except (csv.Error, TypeError) as exc:\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid CSV\") from exc\n\n    if not rows:\n        raise ValueError(\"missing header\")\n\n    header = [name.strip() for name in rows[0]]\n    seen = set()\n    for name in header:\n        if name in seen:\n            raise ValueError(\"duplicate header\")\n        seen.add(name)\n\n    if any(name not in seen for name in _REQUIRED):\n        raise ValueError(\"missing required header\")\n\n    indexes = {name: index for index, name in enumerate(header)}\n    sku_index = indexes[\"sku\"]\n    quantity_index = indexes[\"quantity\"]\n    price_index = indexes[\"unit_price\"]\n\n    aggregates = {}\n    for row in rows[1:]:\n        if len(row) != len(header):\n            raise ValueError(\"row does not match header\")\n\n        sku = row[sku_index].strip()\n        if not sku:\n            raise ValueError(\"empty sku\")\n\n        quantity_text = row[quantity_index].strip()\n        if _INT_RE.fullmatch(quantity_text) is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid quantity\")\n        quantity = int(quantity_text)\n\n        price_text = row[price_index].strip()\n        try:\n            price = Decimal(price_text)\n        except (InvalidOperation, ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid price\") from exc\n        if not price.is_finite() or price < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"invalid price\")\n\n        sign, digits, exponent = price.as_tuple()\n        coefficient = 0\n        for digit in digits:\n            coefficient = coefficient * 10 + digit\n        if sign:\n            coefficient = -coefficient\n\n        term = quantity * coefficient\n        previous = aggregates.get(sku)\n        if previous is None:\n            aggregates[sku] = [quantity, term, exponent]\n        else:\n            total_quantity, total_coefficient, total_exponent = previous\n            if exponent < total_exponent:\n                total_coefficient = (\n                    total_coefficient * (10 ** (total_exponent - exponent)) + term\n                )\n                total_exponent = exponent\n            elif exponent > total_exponent:\n                total_coefficient += term * (10 ** (exponent - total_exponent))\n            else:\n                total_coefficient += term\n            previous[0] = total_quantity + quantity\n            previous[1] = total_coefficient\n            previous[2] = total_exponent\n\n    result = []\n    for sku, (quantity, coefficient, exponent) in aggregates.items():\n        result.append({\n            \"sku\": sku,\n            \"quantity\": quantity,\n            \"revenue\": _revenue_string(coefficient, exponent),\n        })\n    return result\n"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Evidence ev-4ed373a6c4a35a7afa86 | test_ledger.py | lines:1-18 | sha256=fba6a24275abb76d9f6ab51075335968bfe36618cd9fa04271a4ee3d5381e0d9\nimport pytest\nfrom ledger import summarize\n\n\ndef test_aggregate_returns_and_order():\n    assert summarize('sku,quantity,unit_price\\na,2,0.10\\nb,1,3\\na,-1,0.10\\n') == [\n        {'sku': 'a', 'quantity': 1, 'revenue': '0.10'},\n        {'sku': 'b', 'quantity': 1, 'revenue': '3.00'}]\n\n\ndef test_round_only_after_sum():\n    assert summarize('sku,quantity,unit_price\\na,1,0.005\\na,1,0.005\\n')[0]['revenue'] == '0.01'\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('text', ['', 'sku,quantity\\na,1\\n', 'sku,quantity,unit_price\\na,1,NaN\\n'])\ndef test_invalid(text):\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        summarize(text)\n"}], "tool_calls": null, "raw": null, "token_usage": null}], "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_10", "type": "function", "function": {"name": "python_interpreter", "arguments": "plan = [\n    {\"title\": \"Inspect repository and read ledger.py\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Implement summarize in ledger.py\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run full pytest verification\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Finish plan and report result\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n]\nprint(update_plan(plan))"}}], "error": null, "model_output_message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "\n\n```python\nplan = [\n    {\"title\": \"Inspect repository and read ledger.py\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Implement summarize in ledger.py\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run full pytest verification\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Finish plan and report result\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n]\nprint(update_plan(plan))\n```\n\nObservation follows.```", "tool_calls": null, "raw": {"_type"